STATES (every web branch reproduced; each generic P4 leaf state mapped — no hidden DATA section)
  The web leaf is mounted by SystemStatusPage ONLY when update_available is true; it has no internal null/loading
  branch of its own — its only variability is the three optional fragments. Reproducing the source faithfully
  therefore means: the surface is PRESENTED when there is an update (rendering the 3 fragment combinations) and
  WITHDRAWN (EmptyView) for the parent's !hasUpdate absences — the same accepted disposition as 0129 NewVersionBanner
  ("a web parent gate / `return null` maps to a withdrawn native phase, explicitly NOT a hidden section") and 0236
  AccordionSection ("a pure presentational leaf has no fabricated data envelope"). The generic leaf states map as:
    loading  → idle(.awaitingCheck): the update-check has not resolved; the web parent renders nothing until there
               is something to announce. A skeleton callout on every status-page load would be a fabrication the
               web never performs.
    empty    → idle(.upToDate): update_available === false (web `!hasUpdate` → no callout).
    error    → idle(.checkUnavailable): the web parent simply omits the callout on a failed check — reproduced as
               withdrawn, never a visible error box (a QueryError callout here would contradict the source).
    stale    → presented + freshness chip (warning-toned "This result may be out of date"): the web shows the
               callout regardless of staleness; the timestamp is its only freshness cue, promoted to an explicit
               chip + the stale one-shot is owned by the bound source's refresh.
    offline  → presented + freshness chip (muted "Offline — showing the last check"): the cached update is shown
               with an offline annotation (web "cached value + offline chip").
  Plus the three WEB fragment branches, each unit-tested: heading±version, body±current, lastChecked±checkedAt.
  Every idle reason is a distinct, unit-tested classification, even though all render the same faithful withdrawn
  surface.

